<http://data.silknow.org/object/5868a877-08c6-353c-9c1f-d8571116ed55>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Shawl of printed silk and wool gauze, Great Britain, ca. 1845-1860"@en , "Shawl of printed silk and wool gauze. Additional warp and weft stripes of silk are woven in at intervals. The centre of the shawl is plain, but toward each end is a large lozenge-shaped medallion. Around the edges of the field run a series of fantastic cartouches rounding off the corners which are filled with a quarter of the lozenge in the field. The border consists of a series of arcades on a maroon ground. The main colours are turquoise, bright red, bright blue, maroon, black, pink and ochre."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/f7e708d8-c3ef-33a3-94e5-f8226523fc99> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Shawl of printed silk and wool gauze, Great Britain, ca. 1845-1860"@en , "Shawl of printed silk and wool gauze. Additional warp and weft stripes of silk are woven in at intervals. The centre of the shawl is plain, but toward each end is a large lozenge-shaped medallion. Around the edges of the field run a series of fantastic cartouches rounding off the corners which are filled with a quarter of the lozenge in the field. The border consists of a series of arcades on a maroon ground. The main colours are turquoise, bright red, bright blue, maroon, black, pink and ochre."@en ;
